implementationPlan.description:
3. One verification gate, at the end, run once, from WSL in /mnt/d/projexts/moes, in place (launcher harnesses run in place per the global rail). Remove the seat's MOE_*, CLAUDE* and FAKE_* variables (mem:gotcha-qa-ps1-postflight-from-wsl; mem:gotcha-pwsh7-reachable-from-wsl for pwsh.exe), and launch it in the background with job control. The exact command:
`powershell.exe -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File 'D:\projexts\moes\scripts\tests\postflight-vm-route.ps1' && pwsh.exe -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File 'D:\projexts\moes\scripts\tests\postflight-vm-route.ps1' && powershell.exe -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File 'D:\projexts\moes\scripts\tests\worktree-landing.ps1' && bash scripts/tests/parity-check.sh && [ "$(head -c3 scripts/moe-agent.ps1 | od -An -tx1 | tr -d ' \n')" = efbbbf ]`
Required:
- exit 0;
- each PowerShell leg prints its PASS marker with every [vm candidate] and [strong intent] row run. A SKIP line, or an EXIT=0 without the marker, is a failure, never green (see that memory's false-green note);
- worktree-landing.ps1 green and unedited, proving the legacy rounds are unchanged;
- parity PASS: the MOE_VM_ family is not compared until CQ-M07n, and no compared-family code is added;
- the BOM is intact.
The fresh command, exitCode and outputTail are the complete_task evidence.

